---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About">
  <main>

<section class="about-row">

  <div class="about-image">
    <img src="/images/about-photo.webp" alt="Portrait of Dominika">
  </div>

  <div class="about-text">
    <h2>About Me</h2>

    <p>
      I am a wildlife researcher interested in how human activities reshape
      wildlife populations, from their genetic diversity and connectivity
      to their morphology and ecology.
    </p>

    <p>
      My research has taken me from studying the population genetics of
      wolverines across Eurasia to investigating morphological variation
      in wolves. I am particularly interested in how isolation and
      human-driven environmental change affect wildlife, and what these
      changes mean for the animals themselves.
    </p>

    <p>
      I combine field research, population genetics, morphology, and
      quantitative analysis to understand wildlife responses to a changing
      world and to help inform effective conservation.
    </p>

  </div>

</section>

<section class="about-row reverse">

  <div class="about-text">

    <h2>My Journey</h2>

    <p>
      My interest in wildlife started with a fascination for animals 
      and the environments they inhabit. Over time, that interest 
      developed into a scientific focus on understanding how wildlife 
      populations respond to environmental and human-driven change.    
    </p>

    <p>
      Fieldwork and research across different regions have shaped 
      the way I approach ecology: I am interested in the connection 
      between what we can observe in an animal, what is happening 
      within its population, and the broader landscape in which it lives. 
    </p>

  </div>

  <div class="about-image">
    <img src="/images/about_photo2.webp" alt="Fieldwork">
  </div>

</section>


<section class="about-row">

  <div class="about-image">
    <img src="/images/about_photo3.jpg" alt="Fieldwork">
  </div>
  
  <div class="about-text">

    <h2>Beyond Research</h2>

    <p>
      Photography is an important part of how I experience and study 
      wildlife. I see it not simply as a way to document animals, 
      but as a powerful tool for observation, connection, and 
      understanding. Spending time watching and photographing an 
      animal can reveal details of its behaviour, character, 
      interactions, and relationship with its surroundings that can 
      easily be missed.
    </p>

    <p>
      For me, photography creates a different way of looking at 
      wildlife—one that encourages patience, attention, and curiosity. 
      It helps me connect the scientific questions I ask with the 
      animals themselves, and to share that perspective with others.
    </p>


  </div>


</section>

<section class="cv-section">

  <h2>Curriculum Vitae</h2>

  <iframe
    src="/documents/WebCV.pdf"
    width="100%"
    height="900"
    title="Curriculum Vitae">
  </iframe>

</section>


</main>


<style>

main{
    max-width:1200px;
    margin:auto;
    padding:4rem 2rem;
}

.about-row{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
    gap:5rem;
    align-items:center;
    margin-bottom:6rem;
}

.about-row.reverse{
    grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
}

.about-image img{
    width:100%;
    display:block;
}

.about-text h2{
    margin-top:0;
}

.about-text p{
    line-height:1.8;
    font-size:1.05rem;
}
@media (max-width:900px){

.about-row,
.about-row.reverse{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
    gap:2rem;
}

.about-row.reverse .about-image{
    order:-1;
}

}


.cv-section{
    max-width:1300px;
    margin:5rem auto;
}

.cv-section iframe{
    width:100%;
    height:900px;
    border:none;
}

</style>
</Layout>


